  "summary": "Preserve restored dialogue completion flags; release the camp movement/camera circle after the night barrier breaks; stage added guests beyond the original pair before Terror and resume idle guests during that wait.",
  "findings": [
    "An ordinary-play save has b.merc2.n1_2=2 and VCheck#0#10 waiting for it. Unconditional deployment recalculation during explicit loading resets it to 0, leaving the escape unstarted. Explicit restored-VM loads now retain the saved flags; fresh zones and revisits still recalculate topics.",
    "The night escape destroys/removes barrier 1001009. Keeping the safe-zone circle clamps ordinary run-away destinations back into camp. Movement and camera use the released boundary after that phase, while the intact camp/daytime remain bounded.",
    "The first guest staging threshold released Terror while extra actors were still crowding Kir/Kel in the first fireball area. Guests now run past the original marks; the guest gate waits for Y<80. Original Kir/Kel gates, Terror scripts, spells and damage remain unchanged.",
    "A route interrupted by temporary crowding can leave a guest idle before reaching that gate. The active arrival wait reissues only idle guests; active player commands remain in control. This also admits guests arriving after the single original walking order."
  ],
