  "scope": [
    "Production Linux export with actual Lost in Astral assets. Three real ENet host/client runs in one process with separate SceneMultiplayer worlds; headless safe render thread. This is functional validation, not shipping-process/rendering or performance acceptance.",
    "Full escape resumes a copied ordinary-play checkpoint, then runs original AI, attacks, spells, scripts and travel. No actor position/stat/HP injections after load. Initial world ticks are held only while the client joins; HUD dialogue is advanced through normal UI callbacks.",
    "Both clients issuing early run commands, and an idle guest whose host moves on Terror appearing, reach gz1h without any party death. Death signals are checked before transfer because redeployment can revive bodies and hide an in-scene failure.",
    "Client-side camp boundary and camera release are checked on the final ENet run. Two-extra-guest route, idle recovery, player-command retention, fresh-zone recalculation and alive/disconnected gates are isolated in the 29-check movement fixture.",
    "Existing original and Lost in Astral roster/purse/save/name checks pass. No protocol, runtime or native-kernel change."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No full chapter, Internet latency, larger network party or Windows/Android/macOS runtime claim for this follow-up.",
    "Joining over ENet during the middle of the escape wait is not exercised; the isolated fixture covers the corresponding idle-guest recovery behavior.",
    "The save defect is verified at the completed Kel escape dialogue; unrelated saved dialogue sequences are not exhaustively covered.",
    "The scripted escape does not make party members invulnerable or guarantee survival after arbitrary player orders.",
    "Published Experimental 6/tag/assets and device installations are unchanged. Performance work remains deferred."
